@h1 Glossary & cross-references h1@

Every Wit term, defined once, grounded in the AST kinds and source symbols so
guide and reference prose can link a word to its precise meaning. Below the
terms: how to build a glossary or cross-reference set from your own data.

@h2 Nodes and definitions h2@

@dl
@dt Node dt@
@dd A reusable content unit invoked with @@@code @name code@@@; either a
core-vocab built-in or an author definition. dd@

@dt Node use dt@
@dd An invocation of a node (AST @code nodeUse code@); carries a
@code paramsSource code@, a @code closeStyle code@, an optional body, and an
@code inline code@ flag. dd@

@dt Definition dt@
@dd A named template declared with @@@code #name code@@@ (AST
@code nodeDef code@); three shapes — single-line, value-block, block. dd@

@dt Data def dt@
@dd A named value declared with @@@code #name: value code@@@ (AST
@code dataDef code@); its value is a DataValue. dd@

@dt Core vocabulary dt@
@dd The 52 reserved node names that need no definition
(@code CORE_VOCAB_NAMES code@) and ship built-in renderers. dd@

@dt Reserved name dt@
@dd A core-vocab name @strong or strong@ the opaque @code node code@
(@code isReservedNodeName code@); the resolver skips binding lookup for these. dd@

@dt Opaque node dt@
@dd @@@code @node(type X …) code@@@ — a universal pass-through: dispatches to
core vocab if @code type code@ is one, else a @@@code <div data-*> code@@@. dd@

@dt Partial (additive) dt@
@dd A @@@code +#name code@@@ definition that @strong contributes to strong@ a
merged def across the file or project instead of redefining it. dd@
dl@

@h2 Parameters and calls h2@

@dl
@dt Param dt@
@dd A named or positional argument to a node use (AST @code Param code@);
optionally carries a @code typedValue code@. dd@

@dt paramsSource dt@
@dd How a use's params were written: @code parens code@, @code pipes code@,
@code record code@, @code form-fill code@, @code none code@, or
@code mixed code@. dd@

@dt closeStyle dt@
@dd How a use terminates: @code named code@ (a matching close),
@code parens code@ (self-closing), or @code bare code@. dd@

@dt Form-fill dt@
@dd The bare-opener plus @@@code key: value code@@@ lines call form
(@code paramsSource: form-fill code@); needs two or more content lines. dd@

@dt Colon-scatter dt@
@dd A single-line @@@code @name k:v k2:v2 name@ code@@@ body form; classified
internally as @code paramsSource: pipes code@. dd@

@dt Flag param dt@
@dd A valueless param: a trailing bang in a pipe or a bare flag in parens. dd@
dl@

@h2 Data and access h2@

@dl
@dt Record dt@
@dd An ordered key/value map, a brace literal (AST @code record code@); hyphen
delimiter in data-defs, hyphen or colon at call sites. dd@

@dt Collection dt@
@dd An ordered list, a bracket literal (AST @code collection code@). dd@

@dt DataValue dt@
@dd The six-kind value union — string, number, boolean, null, record,
collection — shared by defs, captures, and @code load code@. dd@

@dt Access path dt@
@dd A dotted lookup @@@code @a.b.c code@@@ (AST @code AccessPath code@) with
fuzzy key matching; numeric indexing currently renders unresolved. dd@

@dt Condition dt@
@dd The test in @@@code (if …) code@@@: existence (a path) or a comparison
(@code is code@ / @code equals code@). dd@

@dt Iteration dt@
@dd @@@code (each @collection as item) … (end) code@@@ (AST
@code eachStatement code@); the element is referenced with @@@code @item code@@@. dd@
dl@

@h2 Templating and holes h2@

@dl
@dt Capture dt@
@dd A named hole a def declares (@@@code #name ||a, b|| code@@@), filled by the
caller's params and referenced with @@@code ::a:: code@@@. dd@

@dt Interpolation dt@
@dd @@@code ::name:: code@@@ (AST @code interpolation code@), the substitution
point for a capture. Distinct from the raw hole. dd@

@dt Raw-body interpolation dt@
@dd @@@code {{path}} code@@@ — an expand-time hole valid only inside
@@@code @@ code@@@ raw bodies; supports dotted access; frozen
@@@code @@@ code@@@ disables it. dd@

@dt Body slot dt@
@dd @@@code ... code@@@ (AST @code bodySlot code@), the placeholder in a block
def where the invocation's body is inserted. dd@
dl@

@h2 Raw and reference h2@

@dl
@dt Raw node dt@
@dd @@@code @@name … name@@ code@@@ (@code raw code@): body is one verbatim Text
node, re-interpolated only for @@@code {{…}} code@@@. dd@

@dt Frozen node dt@
@dd @@@code @@@name … name@@@ code@@@ (@code raw + frozen code@): even
@@@code {{…}} code@@@ passes through untouched. dd@

@dt Reference directive dt@
@dd @@@code reference "path" code@@@ — pulls definitions from another file into
the current one. dd@

@dt Script dt@
@dd A @@@code <% … %> code@@@ block or call; effects run at expand, output is
omitted; @code lh code@ is the data bridge. dd@

@dt load dt@
@dd The external-data directive @@@code @load … load@ code@@@; rewritten into a
data def by the load pass before resolve. dd@

@dt DataLoader / DataSource dt@
@dd The host-supplied seam @code load code@ calls — a function or a plain
@@@code { alias: value } code@@@ dictionary. dd@
dl@

@h2 Rendering and pipeline h2@

@dl
@dt Inline-context element dt@
@dd A core element that strips a single leading paragraph from its body
(@code flattenIfInline code@). dd@

@dt Void element dt@
@dd A core element with no body or close — @code br code@, @code hr code@,
@code img code@. dd@

@dt Unresolved fallback dt@
@dd The @@@code <span class="wit-unresolved"> code@@@ a renderer emits for a
name or capture that bound to nothing. dd@

@dt Pipeline stages dt@
@dd @code lex → parse → resolve → expand → render code@; the @code load code@
pass sits between parse and resolve. dd@

@dt Output pathways dt@
@dd The three HTML shapes: @code --fragment code@ (bare article),
@code --raw code@ (reset-only page), default (styled document). dd@
dl@

@h2 Build a glossary from data h2@

Define terms @strong once strong@ as data, then render the list from that source.
Model the glossary as a collection of records and iterate it into a
@code <dl> code@:

@@@pre
#glossary: [
  { term - Attention, gloss - A moral faculty of focus. },
  { term - Fresnel, gloss - A stepped lens for lighthouses. }
]

@dl
(each @glossary as g) @dt @g.term dt@ @dd @g.gloss dd@ (end)
dl@
pre@@@

Read each field with data access — @@@code @g.term code@@@ — not a capture hole.
Edit the data and every view that reads it updates.

@h2 Cross-references and a shared bibliography h2@

Give each referenced thing a unique @code id code@ field and read it wherever you
cite it. Keep the citation call shape uniform so every reference reads the same
way. For a bibliography that assembles across chapter files, combine data with
@a |href /docs/guides/additive-partials/| additive partials a@: each chapter
contributes with @@@code +#bibliography code@@@ and the master renders the merged
node.

@h2 What is not built in h2@

@strong Automatic numbering strong@ ("Figure 3") and @strong back-links strong@
("see above") are @em not em@ core features. Either carry the numbers in your
data, or compute them in a @@@code <% %> code@@@ script (see
@a |href /docs/guides/derived-content/| Derived content a@). The core language
gives the single source of truth and the views; numbering is a renderer or
script concern.

@h2 Common mistakes h2@

@ul
@li Mixing @@@code ::term:: code@@@ and @@@code @g.term code@@@ for the same read
— use data access @@@code @g.term code@@@ outside a definition body. li@
@li Assuming numbering and back-links are automatic — they are not. li@
ul@

